1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,138
This video shows you how to change records with steps,

2
00:00:03,138 --> 00:00:05,950
and with code when steps aren't enough.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,429
Here's the pipeline from the last video.

4
00:00:08,429 --> 00:00:11,910
Each step changes the records that reach it, in order.

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:16,074
DNS lookups to port 53 are noise for this team.

6
00:00:16,074 --> 00:00:18,470
A Drop step removes them.

7
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,818
Drop when the destination port is 53.

8
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:24,112
One record is gone.

9
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:29,669
message is parsed now, so it only repeats the fields.

10
00:00:29,669 --> 00:00:32,220
A Remove step takes it out.

11
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,649
Next, rate each connection's risk.

12
00:00:40,649 --> 00:00:46,470
That depends on several fields at once: the action, the port and the bytes.

13
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:51,870
A Code step runs a short program on each record, for logic like this.

14
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,252
A denied connection to port 22 is high.

15
00:00:55,252 --> 00:00:57,559
Any other denial is medium.

16
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:01,147
An allowed one over 50,000 bytes is watch.

17
00:01:01,147 --> 00:01:03,199
The rest are low.

18
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:06,312
Every record now has a risk.

19
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,810
Save the pipeline.

20
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,029
Now lock this output as a test.

21
00:01:16,029 --> 00:01:20,080
It checks the fields on screen, on all ten rows.

22
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,652
Name it, and lock it.

23
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,946
Samples and review run the test again.

24
00:01:28,946 --> 00:01:34,750
It passes while those fields keep their values, and the dropped record stays dropped.

25
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,681
Check on learning.

26
00:01:36,881 --> 00:01:41,769
A field depends on several other fields, with several cases.

27
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:43,672
Which step fits?

28
00:01:48,072 --> 00:01:49,097
A Code step.

29
00:01:49,097 --> 00:01:54,308
An if and else chain handles the cases in a few lines.

30
00:01:55,208 --> 00:01:58,108
What does a locked test check?

31
00:02:02,508 --> 00:02:07,114
That the pipeline still gives the same values in the locked fields for its sample,

32
00:02:07,114 --> 00:02:09,568
and still drops the same records.

33
00:02:10,468 --> 00:02:14,130
Next, you add fields from lookup tables.
